# Appended by the Vercel/Neon integration, then tidied. `.vercel` was already listed above,
# so only the broader env glob is kept -- with the example negated, because `.env*` matches
# `.env.example`, which IS tracked on purpose. The integration also wrote these lines with
# CRLF, which git reads as the pattern `.env*` and therefore matches nothing at all.
.env*
!.env.example

.vercel
.env*
